{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.PawlowskiLeitnerBasis","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.PawlowskiLeitnerBasis","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Factorial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.clebsch_gordan_half_tensor_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.clebsch_gordan_half_tensor_half","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/pawlowski-leitner-basis.lean#L47-L50","doc":"The Clebsch–Gordan decomposition: dim(V_{1/2}) · dim(V_{1/2}) =\ndim(V_0) + dim(V_1), i.e., 2 · 2 = 1 + 3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiBasis.num_basis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiBasis.num_basis","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/pawlowski-leitner-basis.lean#L45-L45","doc":"The number of basis elements. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiBasis.n_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiBasis.n_ge","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/pawlowski-leitner-basis.lean#L43-L43","doc":"The tensor power is large enough: n ≥ twice_j. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiBasis.parity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiBasis.parity","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/pawlowski-leitner-basis.lean#L41-L41","doc":"Parity constraint: n ≡ twice_j (mod 2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiBasis.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiBasis.n","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/pawlowski-leitner-basis.lean#L39-L39","doc":"The tensor power. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiBasis.twice_j","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiBasis.twice_j","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/pawlowski-leitner-basis.lean#L37-L37","doc":"The spin label (as twice_j). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiBasis.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiBasis.mk","kind":"ctor","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/pawlowski-leitner-basis.lean#L35-L35","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiBasis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiBasis","kind":"structure","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/pawlowski-leitner-basis.lean#L33-L45","doc":"The Pawlowski–Leitner basis structure: specifies the intertwiner\nspace data and the number of basis elements. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:pawlowski-leitner-basis","label":"prop:pawlowski-leitner-basis","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/pawlowski-leitner-basis.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.pawLeiDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.pawLeiDim","kind":"def","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/pawlowski-leitner-basis.lean#L22-L31","doc":"The dimension of the intertwiner space Hom_{SU(2)}(V_j, V_{1/2}^⊗n).\nUses twice_j (so spin j = twice_j / 2).\nReturns 0 when n and twice_j have different parity or n < twice_j.\nRef: [leitnerpawloski2004] https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0409565 ","signatureChunk":0}]}